lisa-addressed:
PERF FIX v2 (measured against the LIVE local-dev dataset: 21 catalogs, 3412 controls, 130 filters, 543k evidences, ~5M evidence_labels). The first CTE-UNION fix was still ~10s live. Root causes found by profiling the live DB:
1. `latest` used `SELECT DISTINCT ON (uuid) * FROM evidences` — a parallel seq scan + external-merge sort of all 543k rows spilling ~24MB to disk (~1s), redone once per 50-filter chunk.
2. Each of 130 filters ran a correlated EXISTS over the ~4895 latest rows (~636k label probes) — 86/130 filters are nested queries.
Fix: replaced the SQL-per-filter approach entirely. Now GetEvidenceStatusCountsByFilters (a) derives `latest` via a LOOSE INDEX SCAN — `SELECT DISTINCT uuid` + lateral latest-per-uuid over the (uuid,"end" DESC) index (no full-table sort) — and LEFT JOINs evidence_labels ONCE (~48k rows, ~450ms), then (b) evaluates every filter in Go via labelfilter.MatchLabels (which mirrors the SQL evaluator, so results are unchanged and stay consistent with profile compliance). componentId scoping folded into the CTE.
Measured on live data: GET /api/lineage/roots 10.15s -> 0.30-0.46s; per-catalog compliance+risk numbers byte-identical to the old path across all 20 catalogs. Integration regression test updated (150 controls/150 filters/5000 evidence now ~40ms, asserts correctness + <5s guard).
